<para id="appendix-b-half-life-source">Half-lives follow <link url="https://doi.org/10.1088/1674-1137/abddae">NUBASE2020</link>, consistent with Appendix A. Parentheses give uncertainty in the last quoted digits. Emission data are rounded selections from the sources below; they may use a different evaluation of branching fractions from NUBASE2020.</para>
<para id="appendix-b-emission-sources">Radiation energies and yields follow the <link url="https://www.lnhb.fr/home/nuclear-data/nuclear-data-table/">DDEP evaluated tables</link>, except for potassium-43, rubidium-86, indium-113m, and mercury-197 (<link url="https://www.lnhb.fr/Laraweb/">LNHB Nucléide-Lara</link>) and cesium-129 (<link url="https://mirdsoft.org/products/MIRDspecs/MIRDspecs_HTMLs/Cs-129.htm">ICRP Publication 107 data reproduced by MIRDspecs</link>). Potassium-43 and rubidium-86 beta endpoints are calculated from the LNHB decay-scheme energy differences. Sodium-22 and potassium-40 branching fractions follow DDEP consistently with their emission data. The sources provide full decay schemes, evaluation dates, and uncertainties. These selected, rounded data are intended for teaching.</para></content>
</document>